<p>Use the following procedure to print the whole page as image data. This 
 allows you to get print results that resemble the display image more closely, 
 but since more data has to be processed printing takes much longer. Use 
 this feature if the printed image differs from the display image.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Whatever the setting made in <span class="Term-Soft">Gray 
 Reproduction:</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> 
 tab, black or gray areas are printed with CMYK toner.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> 
 list, select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
